{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Thus, etc.</b> These too are the words of the prophet, and this is its meaning: Thus said HaShem to me — that I am a despised soul among the wicked. And behold, 'despised' is a noun [adjective] applied to 'soul.'" "<b>To one abhorred by nations.</b> A verb transitive to two objects: that the prophet speaks words for which the nations will abhor him — or 'one abhorred by nations' may mean that the prophet abhors every nation." "<b>To a servant of rulers.</b> The meaning is according to the thought of the exiles of Israel, or it is an allusion to the Babylonians, and this is the correct interpretation." "<b>Kings shall see and arise.</b> I have already hinted to you this sod in the first half of the book (Isaiah 40:1), and according to the opinion of many, kings such as Cyrus, when he hears the words of the prophet, will arise and bow down." "<b>For the sake of YHWH.</b> For he is faithful in his word." "And the kaf of <b>and He chose you</b> forever supports this interpretation."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:44.343785455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}